  "id": "interpersonal-process-recall",
  "term": "interpersonal process recall",
  "definition": "Interpersonal process recall is an interview approach used after therapy or supervision interactions to help participants reflect on what happened in the exchange. In this source, video from natural sessions was used to prompt therapists, clients, and supervisors to recall and discuss subtle relational and emotional processes that might be hard to put into words at the time.",
